  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The hypothesis concerns equiatomic CoCrFeMnNi (Cantor) and related Fe-Co-Ni-based high-entropy alloys in the fcc phase.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6093928::rubric_card::000::eb2c90832c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Static DFT underestimates the cryogenic intrinsic stacking-fault energy of these alloys.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The underestimation occurs because static DFT omits longitudinal spin fluctuations.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Finite-temperature magnetic effects can be modeled using LSF methodology based on DLM theory within EMTO-DFT.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6093928::rubric_card::000::eb2c90832c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The cited calculation spans 50–1200 K and Wigner-Seitz radii of approximately 2.62–2.68 Bohr.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6093928::rubric_card::000::eb2c90832c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ambient-pressure thermal expansion is represented using experimental thermal-expansion data.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6093928::rubric_card::000::eb2c90832c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "LSFs induce finite magnetic moments on Co, Cr, and Ni in CoCrFeMnNi.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6093928::rubric_card::000::eb2c90832c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 100 K in fcc CoCrFeMnNi, the calculated moments are Co = 0.73 μB, Cr = 0.52 μB, and Ni = 0.24 μB.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6093928::rubric_card::000::eb2c90832c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Conventional calculations give zero magnetic moments for Cr and Ni.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6093928::rubric_card::000::eb2c90832c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Conventional static calculations give a zero magnetic moment for Co.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The LSF-induced moments produce magneto-volume coupling.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "LSF-induced moments significantly alter magnetic-entropy and internal-energy contributions to the free energy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "LSFs lead to a negative low-temperature stacking-fault energy because hcp is thermodynamically favored over fcc.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6093928::rubric_card::000::eb2c90832c"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intrinsic stacking-fault energy increases monotonically from about -17 mJ m⁻² at 50 K to about 31 mJ m⁻² at 1000 K.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The predicted fcc-hcp transition temperature is approximately 430 K, compared with approximately 438 K from floating-spin calculations.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The experimental fcc-hcp transition temperature is approximately 633 K.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Explicit phonon effects and structural relaxation of the faulted supercell were omitted.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Comparing static DFT with EMTO-DLM-LSF calculations at 50 K can test whether LSFs generate finite moments and negative stacking-fault energy.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
